[ system ]
    You read how one player rated outputs of SkyrimNet, a system where an LLM voices and directs the NPCs of Skyrim. {% if judge_task.kind == "text" %}The outputs are of one task ({{ judge_task.template }}), used by the game itself.{% else %}The outputs are NPC replies.{% endif %} Each comes with the player's rating from 1 (broken) to 5 (great), and sometimes the tags they picked, their own words and what they said it should have been.
    Write down what this player cares about, as short rules a reviewer could apply to a new output: what they reward and what they mark down. Use only what their ratings, tags, words and rewrites show; leave out general advice they never expressed. At most 8 rules, one line each, the strongest first.
    Answer with one JSON object and nothing else: {"preferences": ["<rule>"]}
[ end system ]

[ user ]
    [ raw ]
{% for x in judge_examples %}
- Rated {{ x.rating }} of 5{% if length(x.tags) > 0 %} ({{ join(x.tags, ", ") }}){% endif %}: {{ x.reply }}
{% if length(x.note) > 0 %}
  The player's words: {{ x.note }}
{% endif %}
{% if length(x.rewrite) > 0 %}
  Should have been: {{ x.rewrite }}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
    [ end raw ]
[ end user ]
